1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:04,990
The cup moves while the model is still processing the previous image.
模型仍在处理上一帧图像时，杯子已经移动了。

2
00:00:05,390 --> 00:00:10,010
Even a correct prediction for that image may now describe the wrong physical situation.
即使对那幅图像的预测是正确的，也可能已经不适用于当前物理情境。

3
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:16,770
Real-time deployment asks when information was captured, when actions were generated, and when they execute.
实时部署要追问：信息何时采集、动作何时生成，以及何时执行。

4
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:21,370
These timestamps connect computation to the changing world around the robot.
这些时间戳，把计算过程与机器人周围持续变化的世界连接起来。

5
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:27,255
A policy that performs well with paused simulation can behave differently when physical time keeps running.
在暂停式仿真中表现良好的策略，在物理时间持续流逝时，可能表现不同。

6
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:32,950
We therefore treat timing as part of the deployed policy, not a cosmetic performance statistic.
因此，我们把时序视为部署策略的一部分，而不是装饰性的性能指标。

7
00:00:33,616 --> 00:00:39,676
Consider a simplified serial example with forty milliseconds of capture and preprocessing delay.
考虑一个简化的串行例子：采集和预处理延迟四十毫秒。

8
00:00:40,496 --> 00:00:46,096
Suppose inference then takes one hundred twenty milliseconds, followed by eighty milliseconds in an action queue.
假设推理再用一百二十毫秒，之后又在动作队列中等待八十毫秒。

9
00:00:46,536 --> 00:00:51,756
The first resulting command uses information that is already two hundred forty milliseconds old.
最终第一条指令使用的信息，就已经是二百四十毫秒之前的了。

10
00:00:52,096 --> 00:00:56,356
This sum is a teaching example, not a latency measurement of any named model.
这个加法是教学例子，不是对任何一个模型的延迟测量。

11
00:00:56,516 --> 00:01:02,496
In an asynchronous system, some intervals overlap, so the real timing diagram must determine the calculation.
在异步系统中，部分区间会重叠，因此必须根据真实时间图进行计算。

12
00:01:02,916 --> 00:01:07,476
Reporting only neural-network inference time would miss important sources of delayed correction.
只报告神经网络推理时间，会漏掉影响延迟纠正的重要来源。

13
00:01:08,144 --> 00:01:14,364
A simple synchronous system predicts a chunk, executes it, and then waits for the next prediction.
简单同步系统先预测一个动作块，执行它，然后等待下一次预测。

14
00:01:15,084 --> 00:01:21,044
During this waiting interval, the robot may stop even when demonstrations contained smooth continuous motion.
在等待区间内，即使示范动作是平滑连续的，机器人也可能停下来。

15
00:01:21,564 --> 00:01:27,484
That pause changes the physical trajectory and can matter for dynamic contact or moving objects.
停顿改变了物理轨迹，对于动态接触或运动物体，可能产生重要影响。

16
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:33,889
Increasing the execution horizon can reduce how often the system pauses, but prolongs open-loop commitment.
增加执行时域，可以减少停顿次数，却也会延长不接受新反馈的执行承诺。

17
00:01:33,904 --> 00:01:38,884
Shortening it can improve opportunities for feedback while increasing inference demands.
缩短执行时域，可以增加接受反馈的机会，但也会增加推理需求。

18
00:01:39,524 --> 00:01:43,804
This is a deployment tradeoff, not something solved by choosing the word chunking.
这是部署中的权衡，不是选用动作分块这个术语就能解决的问题。

19
00:01:44,333 --> 00:01:51,393
In an asynchronous system, the robot executes queued actions while another process predicts future ones.
在异步系统中，机器人执行排队动作，同时另一个进程预测后续动作。

20
00:01:52,053 --> 00:01:57,033
SmolVLA's original diagram separates the robot client from the policy server.
SmolVLA 原图把机器人客户端与策略服务器分开。

21
00:01:57,413 --> 00:02:03,613
A new observation is sent before the current queue empties, allowing inference to overlap execution.
在当前队列清空前发送新观测，让推理与执行发生重叠。

22
00:02:04,193 --> 00:02:08,533
When the response arrives, the system must align it with the actions that remain relevant.
响应到达时，系统必须把它与仍然有效的后续动作对齐。

23
00:02:09,033 --> 00:02:13,598
Otherwise, a numerically valid chunk may start from a state the robot has already left.
否则，一个数值上有效的动作块，可能仍从机器人已经离开的状态出发。

24
00:02:13,613 --> 00:02:19,733
Asynchrony removes some waiting, but does not erase observation age or guarantee smooth switching.
异步消除了一部分等待，但不会消除观测年龄，也不保证切换平滑。

25
00:02:20,299 --> 00:02:25,419
Use another teaching example: a controller runs at fifty updates per second.
再用一个教学例子：控制器每秒更新五十次。

26
00:02:25,699 --> 00:02:31,219
Each action step occupies twenty milliseconds, and inference takes one hundred twenty milliseconds.
每个动作步占用二十毫秒，模型推理需要一百二十毫秒。

27
00:02:31,799 --> 00:02:35,419
Roughly six queued steps will execute while that inference is running.
于是，在这次推理期间，大约有六个排队动作步会被执行。

28
00:02:35,679 --> 00:02:41,479
If a new prediction describes those same timestamps, their values are no longer freely replaceable.
如果新预测涉及这些相同时间戳，它们的数值就不再能够自由替换。

29
00:02:41,699 --> 00:02:48,124
The system should distinguish executed history, committed near-future actions, and a still-editable future suffix.
系统应区分已执行历史、已确定执行的近期动作，以及仍可修改的未来后缀。

30
00:02:48,139 --> 00:02:54,119
That distinction makes queue management a temporal consistency problem rather than a simple list append.
这种区分，让队列管理成为时间一致性问题，而不只是向列表追加元素。

31
00:02:54,728 --> 00:03:00,568
Real-time chunking treats generation of the next action chunk as a constrained inpainting problem.
实时动作分块，把下一段动作的生成视为带约束的补全问题。

32
00:03:01,028 --> 00:03:05,968
The near-future prefix is guided by actions that will execute before inference can finish.
近期前缀由推理完成前就会执行的动作引导。

33
00:03:06,408 --> 00:03:11,028
The remaining suffix can adapt to the latest observation, including the moved cup.
其余后缀则能够适应最新观测，包括被挪动的杯子。

34
00:03:11,288 --> 00:03:16,908
The original timeline shows stronger guidance near committed actions and weaker guidance farther into the future.
原始时间图显示：已确定执行动作附近引导更强，越远的未来引导越弱。

35
00:03:17,248 --> 00:03:21,653
This encourages compatible chunk transitions while retaining room for new corrections.
这样既鼓励动作块平滑衔接，又为新的纠正保留空间。

36
00:03:21,668 --> 00:03:27,928
It is a specific inference method for diffusion or flow policies, not a universal cure for all latency.
这是针对扩散或流策略的具体推理方法，并不是所有延迟问题的通用解药。

37
00:03:28,676 --> 00:03:34,916
Measure capture-to-command delay, action throughput, and task duration as different quantities.
把采集到指令的延迟、动作吞吐量，以及任务时长，作为不同的量测量。

38
00:03:35,356 --> 00:03:41,636
Record the robot, inference hardware, numerical precision, camera resolution, and batch size.
记录机器人、推理硬件、数值精度、相机分辨率，以及批大小。

39
00:03:41,816 --> 00:03:48,116
Also record chunk length, executed steps, network transport, and whether model inputs are cached.
还要记录动作块长度、执行步数、网络传输，以及模型输入是否缓存。

40
00:03:48,336 --> 00:03:53,561
A low average latency can hide occasional stalls that break contact or empty the action queue.
较低平均延迟，可能掩盖偶发停顿；这些停顿会破坏接触，或者耗尽动作队列。

41
00:03:53,576 --> 00:03:59,496
Inspect the latency distribution and missed deadlines, not only the best warmed-up inference call.
应检查延迟分布和错过的期限，而不仅是预热后最好的一次推理。

42
00:03:59,996 --> 00:04:03,536
Parameter count alone cannot recover any of these operational measurements.
仅靠参数量，无法还原这些运行测量。

43
00:04:04,305 --> 00:04:10,465
For a camera-only human interface, we can observe the operator without gloves or wearable trackers.
对于仅用摄像头的人类界面，可以不戴手套或跟踪器，直接观察操作者。

44
00:04:10,805 --> 00:04:16,585
That choice describes human observation; it does not remove the robot's joint encoders or controller.
这个选择描述的是人类观测，并不会移除机器人的关节编码器或控制器。

45
00:04:16,905 --> 00:04:21,865
Nor does every VLA automatically turn visible human motion into a desired robot action.
也并不是每个 VLA 都会自动把可见人类动作，转换成所需机器人动作。

46
00:04:22,145 --> 00:04:28,630
A direct autonomous policy follows its task conditioning, while teleoperation requires an additional intent interface.
直接自主策略遵循其任务条件，而遥操作需要额外的意图接口。

47
00:04:28,645 --> 00:04:34,885
If camera motion is used for demonstrations, its estimates must be mapped into the recorded action contract.
如果用相机观察运动来采集示范，其估计必须映射到记录动作的接口约定。

48
00:04:35,185 --> 00:04:38,885
Keep these modes separate when designing an experiment or labeling a demonstration.
设计实验或标注演示时，应把这些运行模式分清楚。

49
00:04:39,614 --> 00:04:44,974
When the robot misses the cup, inspect the full chain before blaming the action generator.
机器人抓空杯子时，先检查完整链路，不要立刻归咎于动作生成器。

50
00:04:45,674 --> 00:04:51,374
Did the instruction identify the intended cup, and did the image contain enough evidence to locate it?
指令是否指定了正确杯子，图像是否提供了足够的定位证据？

51
00:04:51,814 --> 00:04:56,534
Were action units and frames correct, and did the controller track the decoded reference?
动作单位与坐标是否正确，控制器是否追踪了解码后的参考？

52
00:04:57,074 --> 00:05:01,854
Was the reference current, or was it based on an observation captured before the cup moved?
参考是否仍然有效，还是来自杯子移动之前采集的观测？

53
00:05:02,414 --> 00:05:07,079
Finally, did physical contact fail despite an apparently appropriate reaching motion?
最后，即使接近动作看起来合适，真实接触是否仍然失败？

54
00:05:07,094 --> 00:05:12,954
These questions produce different interventions and prevent one failure label from hiding several causes.
这些问题对应不同改进措施，避免一个失败标签掩盖多种原因。

55
00:05:13,709 --> 00:05:20,189
A selected author video can show that recovery happened, but cannot tell us how reliably it happens.
原作者精选视频可以展示恢复曾经发生，却不能说明恢复有多可靠。

56
00:05:20,909 --> 00:05:26,429
The OpenVLA example shown here contains a reattempt after an unsuccessful interaction with a cup.
这里的 OpenVLA 例子，展示了一次杯子交互不顺利之后的重新尝试。

57
00:05:26,869 --> 00:05:31,354
It is useful qualitative evidence, with the original playback speed clearly labeled.
它是有价值的定性证据，我们会清楚标出原片播放速度。

58
00:05:31,369 --> 00:05:37,629
To measure recovery, define the disturbance, when it occurs, the allowed time, and the success condition.
要测量恢复，应定义扰动内容、发生时刻、允许时间，以及成功条件。

59
00:05:37,989 --> 00:05:42,734
Then repeat trials under comparable resets and retain both successful and failed outcomes.
随后在可比重置条件下重复试验，并保留成功与失败结果。

60
00:05:42,749 --> 00:05:48,889
A retry that eventually drops the cup is not a successful recovery merely because it looked adaptive.
一次重试如果最终摔落杯子，不能因为看起来有适应性，就算作成功恢复。

61
00:05:49,434 --> 00:05:56,974
A deployed system needs explicit behavior when observations disappear, inference stalls, or commands become invalid.
部署系统需要明确规定：观测丢失、推理停顿，或者指令无效时，该怎么做。

62
00:05:57,294 --> 00:06:02,914
Depending on the hardware and task, that may involve a controlled hold, abort, or operator intervention.
根据硬件和任务不同，可能采取受控保持、中止，或者人工介入。

63
00:06:03,374 --> 00:06:09,054
Those choices should be implemented and tested with the actual controller rather than inferred from model confidence.
这些选择应在真实控制器上实现和测试，而不是从模型置信度推断。

64
00:06:09,594 --> 00:06:14,659
A confident token prediction is not a calibrated estimate of collision risk or grasp stability.
高置信度 token 预测，并不是经过校准的碰撞风险或抓取稳定性估计。

65
00:06:14,674 --> 00:06:19,134
Log when an intervention occurs and count its role in the evaluation protocol.
发生介入时应记录下来，并在评估协议中明确它的角色。

66
00:06:19,374 --> 00:06:23,974
Otherwise, an apparently autonomous rollout can quietly depend on unreported assistance.
否则，看似自主的运行，可能悄悄依赖了未报告的帮助。

67
00:06:24,761 --> 00:06:31,681
If failures repeatedly occur after the cup moves, additional static demonstrations may not address the cause.
如果失败总发生在杯子移动之后，增加静态示范未必能解决原因。

68
00:06:32,341 --> 00:06:38,061
First check timing and interfaces, then collect data covering the relevant correction or recovery states.
应先检查时序和接口，再收集覆盖相关纠正或恢复状态的数据。

69
00:06:38,581 --> 00:06:45,061
Supervised fine-tuning can learn from corrected demonstrations, but unsuccessful experience needs appropriate treatment.
监督微调可以学习纠正示范，而失败经验则需要合适的处理方式。

70
00:06:46,141 --> 00:06:52,006
RECAP provides an example of using value and advantage information alongside experience and human corrections.
RECAP 展示了如何把价值与优势信息，同执行经验和人工纠正结合。

71
00:06:52,021 --> 00:06:57,641
The original learning-loop figure separates data collection, value learning, and policy improvement.
原始学习循环图，区分了数据收集、价值学习，以及策略改进。

72
00:06:58,341 --> 00:07:03,501
This is an additional training procedure, not a capability that appears merely by turning on logging.
这是一套额外训练流程，不是打开日志记录就会自动出现的能力。

73
00:07:04,136 --> 00:07:10,756
Producing a finite action tensor is an interface check, not proof of a successful robot task.
产生有限数值的动作张量，是接口检查，不是机器人任务成功的证明。

74
00:07:11,196 --> 00:07:18,076
Playback against recorded observations can reveal gross errors, but does not expose closed-loop distribution shift.
对录制观测回放，可以发现明显错误，却无法暴露闭环分布偏移。

75
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:24,216
A simulator can exercise the control loop under its assumptions, which still differ from physical hardware.
仿真可以在其假设下运行控制环，但这些假设仍与物理硬件不同。

76
00:07:24,676 --> 00:07:29,241
Real execution then tests contact, sensing, delays, and disturbances together.
真实执行随后把接触、感知、延迟和扰动放在一起检验。

77
00:07:29,256 --> 00:07:35,381
A short lift establishes less than transporting, placing, and releasing the cup at the requested location.
短暂提起杯子所证明的内容，少于把它搬运、放置并释放到指定位置。

78
00:07:35,396 --> 00:07:40,156
Label each stage precisely so progress remains useful without overstating completion.
准确标记每个阶段，才能让进展有用，又不夸大完成程度。

79
00:07:40,867 --> 00:07:45,127
Our moved-cup example now has a complete deployment explanation.
到这里，被挪动杯子的例子，已经有了一套完整部署解释。

80
00:07:45,927 --> 00:07:51,767
The observation arrives with an age, the model produces a timed chunk, and the queue commits actions.
观测到达时已有一定年龄，模型生成带时间关系的动作块，队列再确定执行。

81
00:07:52,387 --> 00:07:58,167
The controller realizes those references, while new measurements create opportunities for correction.
控制器执行这些参考，同时新测量带来纠正机会。

82
00:07:58,807 --> 00:08:03,932
Failures become diagnostic data only when we record enough information to locate their cause.
只有记录足够信息来定位原因，失败才会变成有诊断价值的数据。

83
00:08:03,947 --> 00:08:10,887
A deployable model is therefore a model plus interfaces, scheduling, and a verified operating procedure.
所以，可部署模型实际上包含模型、接口、调度，以及经过验证的运行流程。

84
00:08:11,487 --> 00:08:16,527
The final chapter asks how to compare that complete system fairly against meaningful baselines.
最后一章，我们将讨论如何把这个完整系统，与有意义的基线公平比较。
